WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.460
- A California policeman
was intentionally playing

00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:04.780
Taylor Swift during a confrontation

00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:06.630
with a Black Lives Matter activist

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:09.650
with the idea that if they
were playing copyrighted music,

00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:11.550
then the video of this confrontation

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:14.450
could no longer be hosted
on places like YouTube.

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:15.849
- Playing my music so that you can't post

00:00:15.849 --> 00:00:16.900
this on YouTube.
- Is a fucking joke.

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:19.110
- This has hilariously backfired

00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:21.340
because this video is
absolutely everywhere.

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:23.590
But the question is is it
copyright infringement?

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:25.270
And the answer is probably not.

00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:27.310
Though this is a very,
very interesting question

00:00:27.310 --> 00:00:28.750
because when we talk about fair use,

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:30.840
we talk about the recognized categories,

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:33.060
things like commentary,
criticism, and education,

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:34.860
and this doesn't really fall into

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:36.800
any of the enumerated
categories that we know of,

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:39.280
but fair use was specifically designed

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:41.200
by Congress to be non-exclusive.

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:43.690
And I think if this case
ever went to the court,

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:45.277
a judge would take one look at it and say,

00:00:45.277 --> 00:00:46.840
"This is for a political purpose."

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:48.750
There's no copyright
infringement intended,

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:51.200
and, yes, the cop can
try and get away with it,

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:52.033
but they're not going to,

00:00:52.033 --> 00:00:54.990
the video is going to be
promoted pretty much everywhere.

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:56.680
So, if you're a police officer,

00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:58.350
I wouldn't recommend doing this,

00:00:58.350 --> 00:00:59.953
or we'll see you in court.

